How to get your Minecraft .jar
Download and extract the ZIP.
Make sure Java 21 is installed.
Double-click build.bat on Windows while connected to the internet.
Wait for the build to finish.
Find the generated JAR at skull-client/build/libs/skullclient-1.0.0.jar.
Put that JAR into your Minecraft .minecraft/mods folder with Fabric Loader and Fabric API for version 1.21.1.
Important: This download is the build-ready project, not the compiled .jar itself. The build script will attempt to download Gradle and compile it on your computer.
